B.b91=new A.e5("The Year of the Elephant","The hour of birth, and the army that could not enter Makkah.")
B.b8X=new A.e5("The Orphan of Makkah","Father gone before birth, mother at six, grandfather at eight \u2014 and yet al-Amin, the trustworthy.")
B.b8Y=new A.e5("Al-Amin, The Trustworthy","The title Makkah gave him before revelation \u2014 character precedes the call.")
B.b8V=new A.e5("The Cave of Hira","Forty years old, seeking quiet \u2014 and the first word is Iqra.")
B.b96=new A.e5("Iqra \u2014 The First Word","Read, in the name of your Lord. The first revelation chose knowledge.")
B.b8L=new A.e5("Three Years of Whispers","Secret teaching, then open call \u2014 patience measured in years.")
B.b99=new A.e5("Bilal and the Heavy Sand","One word \u2014 Ahad \u2014 heavier than the mountain of sand on his chest.")
B.b8M=new A.e5("The Night of the Journey","From the Haram to Jerusalem to the seven heavens in one night.")
B.b8Z=new A.e5("The Boycott","Three years of siege in the valley \u2014 and the believers stayed.")
B.b8J=new A.e5("The First Hijrah","To Abyssinia, where a just king protected the weak \u2014 Musab carried the message.")
B.b8O=new A.e5("The Conversion of Umar","The man who came to kill left proclaiming \u2014 strength that found its direction.")
B.b94=new A.e5("Taif","Stoned and bleeding, and he prayed for the grandchildren of the people who stoned him.")
B.b97=new A.e5("The Pledges of Aqabah","The people of Yathrib reach for the Prophet \u2014 a city will be renamed after him.")
B.arn=s([B.b91,B.b8X,B.b8Y,B.b8V,B.b96,B.b8L,B.b99,B.b8M,B.b8Z,B.b8J,B.b8O,B.b94,B.b97],t.hN)
B.b8G=new A.Hg("Makkah \u2014 The Formation","Born in the Year of the Elephant, raised an orphan, trusted before he was believed: the Makkan era forms the man. Read these chapters in order \u2014 each one stands alone, together they are a life.",B.arn)
B.b9_=new A.e5("The Hijrah","The cave where a spider\u2019s web and a dove\u2019s nest turned back an empire.")
B.b9b=new A.e5("The Arrival in Madinah","The camel stopped at the place of the masjid \u2014 Quba, then the date-palm land.")
B.b95=new A.e5("The Charter of Madinah","One document binding Muslims, Jews, and pagans of the city \u2014 the first pluralist charter.")
B.b93=new A.e5("The Qibla Changes","From Jerusalem to Makkah \u2014 the direction turns, the meaning deepens.")
B.b8N=new A.e5("Badr: The Two Armies Meet","313 against a thousand \u2014 and Allah\u2019s help came with discipline, not numbers.")
B.b8S=new A.e5("Badr: The Prisoners","The Prophet \ufdfa ransomed literate prisoners by teaching \u2014 the captor became a school.")
B.b90=new A.e5("Uhud: The Day the Line Broke","Fifty archers told to hold a hill \u2014 and the lesson of obedience cost seventy lives.")
B.b98=new A.e5("Uhud: Hamza and the Women","The uncle of the Prophet fell; the women of Uhud did not \u2014 Safiyya on the battlefield.")
B.b8R=new A.e5("The Trench","A city defended with a ditch and words \u2014 Salman\u2019s idea, thirty days of digging.")
B.b8P=new A.e5("Hudaybiyyah","The treaty everyone hated became the conquest of Arabia \u2014 Allah named it a clear victory (48:1).")
B.b8U=new A.e5("Khaybar","After the broken truce, the fortress fell \u2014 and the Prophet ate poisoned food that would carry to his final illness.")
B.b8K=new A.e5("Hunayn and the Return to Taif","Victory over ten thousand at Hunayn, and he went back to the city that stoned him \u2014 to call them again.")
B.alv=s([B.b9_,B.b9b,B.b95,B.b93,B.b8N,B.b8S,B.b90,B.b98,B.b8R,B.b8P,B.b8U,B.b8K],t.hN)
B.b8H=new A.Hg("Madinah \u2014 The Building","The Hijrah turns a persecuted group into a community with a charter, a qibla, and a future. Madinah is where the message learns to build: law, mercy, and the hardest tests of leadership.",B.alv)
B.b8T=new A.e5("The Conquest of Makkah","Ten thousand entered the city of his birth \u2014 and he declared general amnesty.")
B.b8W=new A.e5("Tabuk","The hardest expedition \u2014 nine days\u2019 march in the heat, and the hypocrites exposed by their absence.")
B.b8Q=new A.e5("The Farewell Sermon","No Arab has superiority over a non-Arab \u2014 blood and wealth and honor are sacred: the constitution of the ummah.")
B.b9c=new A.e5("The Passing of the Prophet \ufdfa","He died in Aisha\u2019s arms with his head on her lap, in the room beside the masjid \u2014 and the community learned to live without him.")
B.b9a=new A.e5("What He Left","No silver, no gold, no land \u2014 he left the Qur\u2019an and the example, and they have outlived every empire.")
B.b92=new A.e5("Reflections: The Man Who Walked Beside Us","Aisha was asked about his character; she said: his character was the Qur\u2019an. Read this one last.")
B.akY=s([B.b8T,B.b8W,B.b8Q,B.b9c,B.b9a,B.b92],t.hN)
B.b8I=new A.Hg("The Farewell \u2014 The Completing","Makkah opens without blood, and the Prophet \ufdfa stands at Arafat delivering the sermon that still governs the ummah. The final chapters are the bequest.",B.akY)
B.afk=s([B.b8G,B.b8H,B.b8I],A.a9("y<Hg>"))
B.afl=s(["I. negyed\xe9v","II. negyed\xe9v","III. negyed\xe9v","IV. negyed\xe9v"],t.s)
B.b_v=new A.jg("Ayat al-Kursi \u2014 after Fajr, protection","\u0627\u0644\u0644\u064e\u0651\u0647\u064f \u0644\u064e\u0627 \u0625\u0650\u0644\u064e\u0670\u0647\u064e \u0625\u0650\u0644\u064e\u0651\u0627 \u0647\u064f\u0648\u064e \u0627\u0644\u0652\u062d\u064e\u064a\u064f\u0651 \u0627\u0644\u0652\u0642\u064e\u064a\u064f\u0651\u0648\u0645\u064f \u06da \u0644\u064e\u0627 \u062a\u064e\u0623\u0652\u062e\u064f\u0630\u064f\u0647\u064f \u0633\u0650\u0646\u064e\u0629\u064c \u0648\u064e\u0644\u064e\u0627 \u0646\u064e\u0648\u0652\u0645\u064c","Allah \u2014 there is no god but He, the Ever-Living, the Sustainer. Neither drowsiness nor sleep overtakes Him\u2026 (2:255) \u2014 the Prophet \ufdfa said nothing prevents him who recites it from entering Paradise but death (Nasai).","After each obligatory prayer, and morning/evening.","Qur\u2019an 2:255 \xb7 An-Nasa\u2019i 9927 (wording per Ibn Hibban)")
B.b_H=new A.jg("Sayyid al-Istighfar \u2014 the master of seeking forgiveness","\u0627\u0644\u0644\u064e\u0651\u0647\u064f\u0645\u064e\u0651 \u0623\u064e\u0646\u0652\u062a\u064e \u0631\u064e\u0628\u0650\u0651\u064a \u0644\u064e\u0627 \u0625\u0650\u0644\u064e\u0670\u0647\u064e \u0625\u0650\u0644\u064e\u0651\u0627 \u0623\u064e\u0646\u0652\u062a\u064e \u062e\u064e\u0644\u064e\u0642\u0652\u062a\u064e\u0646\u0650\u064a \u0648\u064e\u0623\u064e\u0646\u064e\u0627 \u0639\u064e\u0628\u0652\u062f\u064f\u0643\u064e","O Allah, You are my Lord; there is no god but You. You created me and I am Your servant\u2026 Whoever says it with conviction morning or evening and dies that day enters Paradise (Bukhari 6306).","Morning and evening.","Bukhari 6306")
B.b_w=new A.jg("Before sleeping","\u0628\u0650\u0627\u0633\u0652\u0645\u0650\u0643\u064e \u0627\u0644\u0644\u064e\u0651\u0647\u064f\u0645\u064e\u0651 \u0623\u064e\u0645\u064f\u0648\u062a\u064f \u0648\u064e\u0623\u064e\u062d\u0652\u064a\u064e\u0627","In Your name, O Allah, I die and I live. The Prophet \ufdfa would place his right hand under his cheek and say it (Bukhari 6314).","On lying down to sleep.","Bukhari 6314")
B.b_x=new A.jg("Before eating","\u0628\u0650\u0633\u0652\u0645\u0650 \u0627\u0644\u0644\u064e\u0651\u0647\u0650","In the name of Allah. The Prophet \ufdfa said: mention Allah\u2019s name, eat with your right hand, and eat from what is nearest (Muslim 2022).","Before the first bite.","Muslim 2022")
B.b_E=new A.jg("The Three Quls \u2014 the evening shield","\u0642\u064f\u0644\u0652 \u0647\u064f\u0648\u064e \u0627\u0644\u0644\u064e\u0651\u0647\u064f \u0623\u064e\u062d\u064e\u062f\u064c \u06dd \u0642\u064f\u0644\u0652 \u0623\u064e\u0639\u064f\u0648\u0630\u064f \u0628\u0650\u0631\u064e\u0628\u0650\u0651 \u0627\u0644\u0652\u0641\u064e\u0644\u064e\u0642\u0650 \u06dd \u0642\u064f\u0644\u0652 \u0623\u064e\u0639\u064f\u0648\u0630\u064f \u0628\u0650\u0631\u064e\u0628\u0650\u0651 \u0627\u0644\u0646\u064e\u0651\u0627\u0633\u0650","Say: He is Allah, One\u2026 Say: I seek refuge in the Lord of daybreak\u2026 Say: I seek refuge in the Lord of mankind (112\u2013114). The Prophet \ufdfa taught them morning and evening three times \u2014 they suffice the servant against everything.","Morning and evening, three times each.","Abu Dawud 5082; Tirmidhi 3575")
B.b_I=new A.jg("Leaving the home \u2014 the morning departure","\u0628\u0650\u0633\u0652\u0645\u0650 \u0627\u0644\u0644\u064e\u0651\u0647\u0650\u060c \u062a\u064e\u0648\u064e\u0643\u064e\u0651\u0644\u0652\u062a\u064f \u0639\u064e\u0644\u064e\u0649 \u0627\u0644\u0644\u064e\u0651\u0647\u0650\u060c \u0648\u064e\u0644\u064e\u0627 \u062d\u064e\u0648\u0652\u0644\u064e \u0648\u064e\u0644\u064e\u0627 \u0642\u064f\u0648\u064e\u0651\u0629\u064e \u0625\u0650\u0644\u064e\u0651\u0627 \u0628\u0650\u0627\u0644\u0644\u064e\u0651\u0647\u0650","In the name of Allah; I place my trust in Allah; there is no might nor power except with Allah (Abu Dawud 5095). Taught as the morning's first sentence when the foot crosses the threshold.","When leaving the house.","Abu Dawud 5095")
B.b_y=new A.jg("After eating \u2014 the thanked meal","\u0627\u0644\u0652\u062d\u064e\u0645\u0652\u062f\u064f \u0644\u0650\u0644\u064e\u0651\u0647\u0650 \u0627\u0644\u064e\u0651\u0630\u0650\u064a \u0623\u064e\u0637\u0652\u0639\u064e\u0645\u064e\u0646\u064e\u0627 \u0648\u064e\u0633\u064e\u0642\u064e\u0627\u0646\u064e\u0627 \u0648\u064e\u062c\u064e\u0639\u064e\u0644\u064e\u0646\u064e\u0627 \u0645\u064f\u0633\u0652\u0644\u0650\u0645\u0650\u064a\u0646\u064e","Praise be to Allah who fed us, gave us drink, and made us Muslims (Tirmidhi 3457). The meal becomes worship when the end matches the beginning.","After finishing a meal.","Tirmidhi 3457")
B.b_A=new A.jg("Entering the home \u2014 the threshold greeting","\u0628\u0650\u0633\u0652\u0645\u0650 \u0627\u0644\u0644\u064e\u0651\u0647\u0650\u060c \u0627\u0644\u0644\u064e\u0651\u0647\u064f\u0645\u064e\u0651 \u0625\u0650\u0646\u0650\u0651\u064a \u0623\u064e\u0633\u0652\u0623\u064e\u0644\u064f\u0643\u064e \u062e\u064e\u064a\u0652\u0631\u064e \u0627\u0644\u0652\u0645\u064e\u0648\u0652\u0644\u064e\u062c\u0650 \u0648\u064e\u062e\u064e\u064a\u0652\u0631\u064e \u0627\u0644\u0652\u0645\u064e\u062e\u0652\u0631\u064e\u062c\u0650","In the name of Allah. O Allah, I ask You for the good of entering and the good of leaving (Abu Dawud 5096). The home is entered with His name, not with the day's residue.","When entering the house.","Abu Dawud 5096")
B.b_F=new A.jg("Entering the mosque \u2014 asking the doors of mercy","\u0627\u0644\u0644\u064e\u0651\u0647\u064f\u0645\u064e\u0651 \u0627\u0641\u0652\u062a\u064e\u062d\u0652 \u0644\u0650\u064a \u0623\u064e\u0628\u0652\u0648\u064e\u0627\u0628\u064e \u0631\u064e\u062d\u0652\u0645\u064e\u062a\u0650\u0643\u064e","O Allah, open for me the doors of Your mercy (Muslim 713). Said with the right foot at the mosque's door.","Entering the mosque.","Sahih Muslim 713")
B.b_z=new A.jg("After the prayer \u2014 the closing words","\u0623\u064e\u0633\u0652\u062a\u064e\u063a\u0652\u0641\u0650\u0631\u064f \u0627\u0644\u0644\u064e\u0651\u0647\u064e (\xd7\u0663) \u0627\u0644\u0644\u064e\u0651\u0647\u064f\u0645\u064e\u0651 \u0623\u064e\u0646\u0652\u062a\u064e \u0627\u0644\u0633\u064e\u0651\u0644\u064e\u0627\u0645\u064f \u0648\u064e\u0645\u0650\u0646\u0652\u0643\u064e \u0627\u0644\u0633\u064e\u0651\u0644\u064e\u0627\u0645\u064f","I seek Allah's forgiveness (three times). O Allah, You are Peace and from You comes peace\u2026 (Muslim 591). The prayer does not end; it hands you to the next worship.","After each obligatory prayer.","Sahih Muslim 591")
B.b_D=new A.jg("Boarding any transport \u2014 the borrowed ride","\u0633\u064f\u0628\u0652\u062d\u064e\u0627\u0646\u064e \u0627\u0644\u064e\u0651\u0630\u0650\u064a \u0633\u064e\u062e\u064e\u0651\u0631\u064e \u0644\u064e\u0646\u064e\u0627 \u0647\u064e\u0670\u0630\u064e\u0627 \u0648\u064e\u0645\u064e\u0627 \u0643\u064f\u0646\u064e\u0651\u0627 \u0644\u064e\u0647\u064f \u0645\u064f\u0642\u0652\u0631\u0650\u0646\u0650\u064a\u0646\u064e","Glory to Him who subjected this to us, and we could never have accomplished it ourselves (43:13). The Prophet \ufdfa recited it mounting his ride, then said Allahu Akbar three times (Muslim 1342).","Boarding a vehicle, mount, or seat of travel.","Qur'an 43:13; Sahih Muslim 1342")
B.b_B=new A.jg("In distress \u2014 the dua of the afflicted","\u0644\u064e\u0627 \u0625\u0650\u0644\u064e\u0670\u0647\u064e \u0625\u0650\u0644\u064e\u0651\u0627 \u0627\u0644\u0644\u064e\u0651\u0647\u064f \u0627\u0644\u0652\u0639\u064e\u0638\u0650\u064a\u0645\u064f \u0627\u0644\u0652\u062d\u064e\u0644\u0650\u064a\u0645\u064f\u060c \u0644\u064e\u0627 \u0625\u0650\u0644\u064e\u0670\u0647\u064e \u0625\u0650\u0644\u064e\u0651\u0627 \u0627\u0644\u0644\u064e\u0651\u0647\u064f \u0631\u064e\u0628\u064f\u0651 \u0627\u0644\u0652\u0639\u064e\u0631\u0652\u0634\u0650 \u0627\u0644\u0652\u0639\u064e\u0638\u0650\u064a\u0645\u0650","There is no god but Allah, the Magnificent, the Forbearing; there is no god but Allah, Lord of the Mighty Throne (Bukhari 6346). The Prophet \ufdfa taught it to the distressed as a prayer Allah does not refuse.","In any hardship, anxiety, or tightness of the chest.","Sahih al-Bukhari 6346")
B.b_C=new A.jg("Hasbunallahu wa ni'mal wakil \u2014 the sufficiency clause","\u062d\u064e\u0633\u0652\u0628\u064f\u0646\u064e\u0627 \u0627\u0644\u0644\u064e\u0651\u0647\u064f \u0648\u064e\u0646\u0650\u0639\u0652\u0645\u064e \u0627\u0644\u0652\u0648\u064e\u0643\u0650\u064a\u0644\u064f","Allah is sufficient for us, and He is the best Disposer of affairs (3:173) \u2014 the words of Ibrahim's household at the fire and of the Prophet \ufdfa at Uhud. Spoken, the chest loosens.","When facing what you cannot control.","Qur'an 3:173")
B.b_G=new A.jg("The master of forgiveness \u2014 morning anchor","\u0627\u0644\u0644\u064e\u0651\u0647\u064f\u0645\u064e\u0651 \u0623\u064e\u0646\u0652\u062a\u064e \u0631\u064e\u0628\u0650\u0651\u064a \u0644\u064e\u0627 \u0625\u0650\u0644\u064e\u0670\u0647\u064e \u0625\u0650\u0644\u064e\u0651\u0627 \u0623\u064e\u0646\u0652\u062a\u064e\u060c \u062e\u064e\u0644\u064e\u0642\u0652\u062a\u064e\u0646\u0650\u064a \u0648\u064e\u0623\u064e\u0646\u064e\u0627 \u0639\u064e\u0628\u0652\u062f\u064f\u0643\u064e","O Allah, You are my Lord; there is no god but You. You created me and I am Your servant\u2026 (Bukhari 6306). Whoever says it with conviction in the morning or evening and dies that day or night enters Paradise.","Morning and evening.","Sahih al-Bukhari 6306")
